## UI

- Responsive
- Mobile friendly
- Accessible
- Consistent spacing
- Consistent typography
- Page headers must always be breadcrumbs via `PageHeader` / `PageBreadcrumb`. Never use a title + description block as the page header.

### default-win-form

- Default shell name: `default-win-form`. `FormPanel` always applies it; custom markup using `default-win-form` / `default-win-form__*` gets the same styling.
- Primary actions: `defaultWinForm.buttonPrimary` (or `default-win-form__button default-win-form__button--primary`).
- Prefer that chrome over ad-hoc bordered cards.
- **Final spacing (do not change without explicit user request).** Source of truth: `frontend/src/styles/forms.css`.

Sizing tokens on `.default-win-form`:

- Inputs: `--form-control-font-size: 0.9375rem`, `--form-control-line-height: 1.35`, `--form-control-pad-y: 0.45rem`, `--form-control-pad-x: 0.75rem`
- Buttons (separate from inputs): `--form-button-pad-y: 0.35rem`, `--form-button-pad-x: 0.6rem` — do not inherit input padding or input height
- Header/footer bars (equal height): `--form-bar-pad-y: 0.45rem`, `--form-bar-min-height: calc(var(--form-control-height) + (var(--form-bar-pad-y) * 2))`
- Body: `0.85rem` padding; fields: `0.28rem` label gap, `0.65rem` field spacing
- Wide variant body: `0.65rem 0.7rem`; wide header/footer inline: `0.7rem`
- Depth: Yoradm-style inset top rim (`box-shadow: 0 1px 0 … inset`), not drop shadow

Rules:

- Header and footer share `--form-bar-min-height` and `--form-bar-pad-y`; footer padding is outside the button, not inside it
- `--form-control-height` is derived from input font/line-height/padding; bars grow with it automatically
- Never shrink footer buttons to fit bar height; keep compact button padding tokens instead
- Every `default-win-form` header should include an appropriate semantic icon via `FormPanel`'s `titleIcon` prop
- Reuse the shared header icon size from `.default-win-form__title-icon`; keep it consistent at `1.15rem` instead of one-off per-form sizing
- **Icons: Heroicons only** (`@heroicons/react/24/outline`). Import from `frontend/src/components/forms/formIcons.tsx`; never add custom inline SVG icons for forms, settings, or modals

### Icons

- Use **Heroicons** outline (`@heroicons/react/24/outline`) exclusively for UI icons in forms, settings, and modals
- Re-export shared icons from `frontend/src/components/forms/formIcons.tsx` so naming stays consistent across the app
- Do not hand-draw or copy ad-hoc SVG paths; add new icons via Heroicons and export them from `formIcons.tsx`

### Settings

Settings open as a modal (`SettingsModal` via `useSettings().openSettings()`), not as a content-section page — same pattern as Yoradm. Sidebar Settings is a button, not a route. `/settings` and `/users` open the modal then navigate home.

### Tables

All data tables must use the Yoradm-style `app-table` pattern from `frontend/src/index.css`. Do not invent one-off Tailwind table layouts.

Required markup — sticky header, scrollable body, fixed footer:

```tsx
<div className="app-table-wrap app-table-shell">
  <div className="app-table-scroll">
    <table className="app-table">
      <thead>
        <tr>
          <th>Column</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Value</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <div className="app-table-foot">
    <span className="app-table-foot-label">1 row</span>
  </div>
</div>
```

Rules:

- Always use `app-table-shell` + `app-table-scroll` + `app-table-foot`. Header stays fixed via sticky `thead`; body scrolls in `app-table-scroll`; footer stays fixed below the scroll area.
- Wrap bordered page tables in `app-table-wrap` (bordered, rounded). Flush/tab tables (e.g. Settings Users) may use `app-table-shell` without the wrap.
- Every table must include an `app-table-foot` (count, totals, or status). Do not omit it.
- Use `app-table` on the `<table>` (sticky muted headers, compact cells, hairline row dividers).
- In-row selects use `app-table-select` — not ad-hoc bordered selects.
- Numeric / ID columns use `app-table-num` (right-aligned, tabular nums via mono).
- Empty / loading / error states inside the scroll area use `app-table-empty` (or a single empty `<td colSpan={…} className="app-table-empty">`).
- Prefer extending `app-table*` in `index.css` over page-local table CSS when a new shared variant is needed.

Reference: Settings Users (`frontend/src/components/settings/UsersPanel.tsx`) and Yoradm `win-form__table-shell`.

